# User-facing copy (i18n / orthography)

Applies to **every** user-visible string on tourai.es — not only What's New.

## Where copy lives (web)

| Kind | Location |
|------|----------|
| Static page copy (marketing, legal, FAQ body) | Root `*.html` (Spanish) and `en/*.html` (English) |
| Dynamic UI (auth, account, forms, community, reviews) | `js/locales/es-ES.js` / `en-GB.js` via `t()` / `tOr()` |

Do not bury new Spanish/English UI sentences only inside JS when a locale key should exist. Do not reintroduce `data-i18n` on public HTML for page body copy.

App chrome for the same feature lives in TourAI `.resx` (see TourAI `user-facing-copy.mdc`).

## Spanish orthography (mandatory)

All Spanish copy (HTML, locales, legal bodies): correct accents and ñ (`menú`, `versión`, `información`, `Síguenos`, `Perelló`, …). Spot-check after edits; fix mojibake immediately. UTF-8 without BOM — see `utf8-file-encoding.mdc`.

## Checklist

- [ ] New/changed static strings edited in **both** ES and EN HTML when the page is public in both languages
- [ ] New/changed dynamic strings use locale keys in **both** `es-ES.js` and `en-GB.js`
- [ ] Spanish accents correct
